 ## Data file schemas (under `./shopkeep-data/`)
 
-### products.csv  (rewritten atomically on stock changes)
+### products.csv  (10 columns; rewritten atomically on stock changes)
 ```
-barcode,name,price_paise,qty,threshold,description,type,image
+barcode,name,price_paise,qty,threshold,description,type,image,expiry_date,hsn_code
 ```
 - `type` is the product's CATEGORY — it files the product into its category
   tray. Unknown types auto-create a tray with a matching emoji.
@@ -80,17 +133,32 @@ barcode,name,price_paise,qty,threshold,description,type,image
   (EAN-13 prefix 20–29 is the globally reserved in-store range — same trick
   real POS systems use), so every product is scannable.
 - `price_paise` — integer paise (Rs 25.00 = 2500). No floats anywhere.
+- `expiry_date` — `YYYY-MM-DD`, drives the `expiry` report and dashboard flags.
+- `hsn_code` — HSN classification for GST-ready receipts.
+- Old 5-column and 8-column files auto-migrate on first write.
 - Names may contain commas and quotes (proper RFC-4180-style CSV quoting).
 
-### bills.csv  (append-only ledger — rows are NEVER edited or deleted)
+### bills.csv  (10 columns; append-only ledger — rows are NEVER edited or deleted)
 ```
-bill_no,timestamp,barcode,name,qty,unit_price_paise,line_total,action
+bill_no,timestamp,barcode,name,qty,unit_price_paise,line_total,action,phone,discount_paise
 ```
 - ONE ROW PER LINE ITEM, not per bill (mirrors how real POS databases normalize).
 - `name` + `unit_price_paise` are copied INTO the row so historical bills stay
   correct even after a price change later (audit history).
 - `action` is `SELL` or `VOID`. Voiding appends `VOID` rows for the bill's line
   items and restores stock — nothing is ever deleted.
+- `phone` is the customer's normalised mobile (`919876543210`), so bills are
+  queryable by customer. `discount_paise` is the per-line discount applied.
+- **1:1 reconcile:** every committed `SELL` row has exactly one matching
+  `SALE` row in `inventory_log.csv` (detail `bill=<bill_no>`). VOID reversal
+  rows are logged the same way.
+
+### inventory_log.csv
+```
+timestamp,event,barcode,name,qty,price_paise,detail
+```
+Events: `ADD` `EDIT` `RESTOCK` `REMOVE` `SALE` `VOID` `RETURN` `STOCKVALUE`
+`TRAY_NEW` `TRAY_ADD` `TRAY_REMOVE` `PUBLISH`.
 
